  "categories": [
    "QEI Clinic"
  ],
  "hero": "wp-content/uploads/2026/03/eBook-Mockup-1-1430x1033.png",
  "hero_alt": "",
  "excerpt": "",
  "body_html": "<p>A new publication by QEI’s Dr Brendan Cronin and Dr Rebecca Cox aims to improve care from the moment patients first engage with an ophthalmology clinic. The publication offers practical tips for medical receptionists, definitions of important ophthalmic terms and a thorough overview of eye conditions and treatments.</p>\n<p><a href=\"../../introduction-to-ophthalmology-for-medical-receptionists\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Mockup showing front cover and a two-page spread from publication\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-6533 size-large\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"463\" id=\"longdesc-return-6533\" longdesc=\"https://qei.org.au?longdesc=6533&amp;referrer=6532\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/eBook-Mockup-1-1024x740.png\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/eBook-Mockup-1-1024x740.png 1024w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/eBook-Mockup-1-300x217.png 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/eBook-Mockup-1-768x555.png 768w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/eBook-Mockup-1-1536x1109.png 1536w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/eBook-Mockup-1-2048x1479.png 2048w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/eBook-Mockup-1-1430x1033.png 1430w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/eBook-Mockup-1-800x578.png 800w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/eBook-Mockup-1-400x289.png 400w\" tabindex=\"-1\" width=\"640\"/></a></p>\n<p>Dr Cronin says medical receptionists are critical to a patient’s eye care journey and he was surprised he couldn’t find any educational resources dedicated to them when he searched.</p>\n<p>“Ophthalmology clinics offer unique challenges to reception staff,” Dr Cronin says.</p>\n<p>“There’s a huge number of potential diseases in the eye, so working in an ophthalmology clinic is like working for multiple different types of surgeons,” he says.</p>\n<p>“It just makes sense to me that training receptionists to understand what we do and what patients experience will not only make their job more enjoyable it will also make them better at it.”</p>\n<p>Available to purchase here: <a href=\"../../introduction-to-ophthalmology-for-medical-receptionists\">Introduction to Ophthalmology for Medical Receptionists | Queensland Eye Institute</a></p>\n<p> </p>\n<figure aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-6534\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\" id=\"attachment_6534\" style=\"width: 640px\"><img alt=\"A man in maroon medical scrubs leans against a reception counter. Behind the counter some women in navy medical scrubs are talking or working at computer screens.\" class=\"wp-image-6534 size-large\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"480\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/20240717_QEI-BrendanCronin_Reception-1_Web-1024x768.jpg\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/20240717_QEI-BrendanCronin_Reception-1_Web-1024x768.jpg 1024w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/20240717_QEI-BrendanCronin_Reception-1_Web-300x225.jpg 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/20240717_QEI-BrendanCronin_Reception-1_Web-768x576.jpg 768w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/20240717_QEI-BrendanCronin_Reception-1_Web-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/20240717_QEI-BrendanCronin_Reception-1_Web-2048x1536.jpg 2048w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/20240717_QEI-BrendanCronin_Reception-1_Web-1430x1073.jpg 1430w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/20240717_QEI-BrendanCronin_Reception-1_Web-800x600.jpg 800w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2026/03/20240717_QEI-BrendanCronin_Reception-1_Web-400x300.jpg 400w\" width=\"640\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\" id=\"caption-attachment-6534\">Dr Brendan Cronin at the Woolloongabba clinic reception counter</figcaption></figure>",
